<div class="page-hero wrap reveal">
  <span class="eyebrow">Approach</span>
  <h1>Mechanism creates possibility. Experience creates perception. Context shapes interpretation.</h1>
  <p>Most companies optimise at one level. The best create an aligned feel-state across all three — here's the full framework and how a project actually moves through it.</p>
</div>

<section style="padding-top:0;">
  <div class="wrap reveal">
    <span class="eyebrow">The DNA framework</span>
    <h2 class="section-title">Three truths, one feel-state.</h2>
    <div class="dna-wrap">
      <div class="dna-card">
        <span class="dna-num">01 — Mechanical Truth</span>
        <h3>What's physically and biologically occurring.</h3>
        <p>The objective, molecular, and physical realities of the product, and the baseline biological state of the human body — the domain of physicists, chemists, and formulation engineers.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="dna-card">
        <span class="dna-num">02 — Experiential Truth</span>
        <h3>What's consciously perceived and felt.</h3>
        <p>The relationship between sensory stimulation, nervous-system activation, and subjective emotional response — the domain of sensory science, neuromechanics, and cognitive psychology.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="dna-card">
        <span class="dna-num">03 — Contextual Truth</span>
        <h3>What shapes interpretation and behaviour.</h3>
        <p>The invisible social architectures, cultural norms, and situational terrain that govern any moment — the domain of behavioural psychology, anthropology, and semiotics.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="dna-connector">Together, they create meaning — and an unmistakable feel-state DNA.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

